n exciting year for researchers: both RLVR and GRPO are conceptually intere=
sting and, depending on scale, not prohibitively expensive to experiment wi=
th.</p><p>So, there have been many mathematical improvements to GRPO that I=
 saw in the LLM research literature this year (from both companies and acad=
emic researchers), which were later adopted in the training pipelines of st=
ate-of-the-art LLMs. For instance, some of the improvements include the fol=
lowing:</p><p><strong><a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.13961">Olmo 3</=
a><span>:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span>Zero gradient signal filterin=
g (DAPO by </span><a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.14476">Yu et al., 2=
025</a><span>)</span></p></li><li><p><span>Active sampling (DAPO by </span>=
<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.14476">Yu et al., 2025</a><span>)</sp=
an></p></li><li><p><span>Token-level loss (DAPO by </span><a href=3D"https:=
//arxiv.org/abs/2503.14476">Yu et al., 2025</a><span>)</span></p></li><li><=
p><span>No KL loss (DAPO by </span><a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.14=
476">Yu et al., 2025</a><span> and Dr. GRPO by </span><a href=3D"https://ar=
xiv.org/abs/2503.20783">Liu et al., 2025</a><span>)</span></p></li><li><p><=
span>Clip higher (DAPO by </span><a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.1447=
6">Yu et al., 2025</a><span>)</span></p></li><li><p><span>Truncated importa=
nce sampling (</span><a href=3D"https://fengyao.notion.site/off-policy-rl">=
Yao et al., 2025</a><span>)</span></p></li><li><p><span>No standard deviati=
on normalization (Dr. GRPO by </span><a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.=
20783">Liu et al., 2025</a><span>)</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><a href=
=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.02556">DeepSeek V3.2</a><span>:</span></stro=
ng></p><ul><li><p>KL tuning with domain=E2=80=91specific KL strengths (zero=
 for math)</p></li><li><p>Reweighted KL</p></li><li><p>Off=E2=80=91policy s=
equence masking</p></li><li><p>Keep sampling mask for top=E2=80=91p / top=
=E2=80=91k</p></li><li><p>Keep original GRPO advantage normalization</p></l=
i></ul><p>I can confirm that these GRPO tricks or modifications have a huge=
 impact in practice. For instance, with some or multiple of these modificat=
ions in place, bad updates no longer corrupt my training runs, and I no lon=
ger need to reload checkpoints periodically.</p><p>And even for very short =
